## Running them

Everything: `{{TEST_COMMAND}}`
A single file: `{{TEST_SINGLE_COMMAND}}`

Prefer `scripts/ci.sh` over calling the framework directly — `fast` for the per-subtask check, `full` before a merge or release. It is the same script CI runs — provided every command in it resolves through the package manager rather than a globally installed binary, which is what `/project-init`'s clean-clone check verifies.

Framework: {{TEST_FRAMEWORK}}

## Layout

Tests are split by **level** first, then mirror `src/` inside each level — `src/auth/oauth.ts` → `tests/unit/auth/oauth.test.ts`, and its integration counterpart → `tests/integration/auth/oauth.test.ts`. `scripts/ci.sh` runs `tests/unit` in `fast` and adds `tests/integration` in `full`, so a test in the wrong directory runs at the wrong time — or, in the case of a slow integration test under `tests/unit/`, on every single subtask.

